HEAP 
A heap is a complete binary tree that follows a specific ordering property. In a min heap, the smallest element is always at the root, and in a max heap, the largest element is always at 
the root. When we remove the root, the heap rearranges itself to maintain the heap property

PRIORITY QUEUE 
“A priority queue is a data structure in which elements are processed based on their priority rather than their insertion order. It is commonly implemented using a heap.

